 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+The error-hook behavior below is recorded for future hook features and remains outside issue #93.
 
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
+
+## Turn usage — issue #93
+
+The chosen contract keeps one summed `usage` argument. A per-round breakdown is deferred because this issue's billing and budgeting consumers need a turn total; adding a second representation widens the API without serving that requirement. The public hook signature must name the argument or its type as a turn total. This behavior change requires a MINOR bump and a changelog entry explaining that existing consumers now record larger totals for tool turns. The existing no-tool test `receives collected response text and usage` stays unedited.
+
+- `afterModelResponse` fires once per user message after the round loop and receives the sum of `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, and `totalTokens` from every provider call, including both tool rounds and the final answer. ([validated by: reports the sum of all three provider calls across two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L72)).
+- Missing usage on any round is ignored while all reported rounds are summed; if no round reports usage, the hook receives `undefined`, and totals never carry into another turn. ([validated by: sums reported rounds despite missing usage and reports nothing when every round omits it](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestratorUsage.acceptance.test.ts#L82)).
